// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 08-alias-validity
// facility: rule.value-object.read [Read-Conflict]; conf.reborrow-ok (derivation note)
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (static)
//
// A read through the owner while an exclusive descendant is live is
// [Read-Conflict] (spec/conformance.md, conf.reborrow-ok: "reading x
// itself here would be [Read-Conflict]"). Before the fix, the write
// through `r` had already disabled `r` as a conflict witness for `x`.

fn main()
{
    i32 x = 1;
    auto r = &mut x;
    *r = 5;
    i32 y = x;
}
